    <!-- ===================== Context menu icon set (guide Part 3) =====================
         Hand-converted from icon-menu.md (24x24 viewBox, stroke="#1C274C" /
         stroke-width="1.5" line icons, a few solid-fill glyphs). Each entry
         is a DataTemplate rather than a bare Geometry, because several icons
         mix stroke-only and fill-only sub-shapes (e.g. Inspect's two circles
         + five strokes, Add to Mozart's two solid dot "eyes"), which a single
         Geometry+Fill/Stroke pair can't represent on its own.

         Consumed from ContextMenuBuilder.RenderEntry via
         Application.Current.TryFindResource(entry.IconKey), wrapped in a
         fresh ContentControl per MenuItem so each gets its own instantiation
         of the visual tree.

         Sizing: each <Viewbox> below has no explicit Width/Height - it
         stretches to fill whatever size the icon ContentPresenter in
         ControlStyles.xaml's MenuItem template gives it (currently 22x22,
         bumped 2026-08-22 from 16x16 for a bigger/easier-to-read menu
         overall). Changing the menu's icon size in the future only needs
         that one ContentPresenter Width/Height changed, not all 25 of these.

         Color: every Stroke/Fill below binds to TextSecondaryBrush (already
         defined in Themes/Light.xaml + Dark.xaml) instead of the source
         SVGs' literal #1C274C, so one resource swap re-themes every icon
         automatically. -->

